MIOpen (rocm-libraries release/therock-10.2): restore the gfx803 Winograd
convolution solvers.

WHY
---
Upstream commit 994fed065e "fix(miopen): remove gfx803-tuned solvers and stale
kernel sources (#11761)" removes every forward and backward-data Winograd path
that MIOpen has for gfx803:

  * ConvBinWinogradRxSFused, the fused Conv+Bias+Activation Winograd solver, is
    deleted with its GCN3 kernels (conv_3x3_wheel_alpha_v9_2_7*).
  * ConvBinWinograd3x3U loses its gfx803 branch and its GCN3 kernel
    (conv_3x3_wheel_alpha_v3_0b*).
  * ConvBinWinogradRxS loses gfx803 for forward and backward data, and
    conv_3x3_wheel_alpha_v9_0_15*.s lose their gfx8 bodies (*_gfx8*.inc).
  * The gfx803 find-db files (gfx803_36.HIP.fdb.txt.bz2,
    gfx803_64.HIP.fdb.txt.bz2) are deleted, and gfx803 leaves
    ALL_GPU_DATABASES.

Without this patch, a gfx803 convolution can run only on these solvers: the asm
and OpenCL direct-convolution solvers, GEMM through rocBLAS, the non-xdlops HIP
implicit-GEMM solvers, ConvWinograd3x3MultipassWrW (weight gradient only), and
the naive reference kernels. Every other Winograd solver in this tree
(ConvBinWinogradRxSf2x3, ConvBinWinogradRxSf2x3g1, ConvWinoFuryRxS,
ConvWinoRageRxS, ConvMPBidirectWinograd) checks for gfx9 or later in
IsApplicable. Nobody has measured the throughput difference on gfx803 between
the solver set with this patch and the solver set without it.

The restored solver and kernel sources are byte-identical to
release/therock-10.1 (39d8d60365). The one exception is the marker comment in
conv_bin_wino3x3U.cpp. The same files are also byte-identical in
release/therock-10.0, and the per-solver gfx803 sweeps in
winograd-fused-conv-miscompute.patch ran on that line (ConvBinWinogradRxS 17
shapes and ConvBinWinograd3x3U 18 shapes, 0 wrong). The ROCm 10.1 image that
passed tools/imgvalidate.sh on the card carried these solvers too.

ConvBinWinograd3x3U and ConvBinWinogradRxS report no WTI estimate, and neither
is in the solver list of MIOpen's immediate-mode ranking model. So when the
find-db has no entry for a problem, immediate mode does not pick them. They run
when Find benchmarks them (the default DynamicHybrid find mode does this on a
find-db miss), when a user find-db entry names them, or when
MIOPEN_DEBUG_FIND_ONLY_SOLVER forces them. ConvBinWinogradRxSFused is chosen by
its own WTI inside a fusion plan.

WHAT
----
This is the reverse of 994fed065e for the library sources:

  * src/solver/conv_bin_winoRxS_fused.cpp, its declaration in
    include/miopen/fusion/solvers.hpp, its place in GetFusedWinogradSolvers()
    (fusion.cpp), and its registration in solver.cpp, under the solver ID it
    held before.
  * The gfx803 branches of ConvBinWinograd3x3U and ConvBinWinogradRxS.
  * The deleted GCN3 kernel sources, their entries in src/CMakeLists.txt, and
    the gfx8 branch of the three conv_3x3_wheel_alpha_v9_0_15*.s files.

The patch does not restore these parts of the commit:

  * Docs, tests and the CHANGELOG entry. The library build reads none of them.
  * legacy_ck_common.hpp's is_ck_supported_hardware(). Nothing in the tree
    calls it.
  * The find-db files and the gfx803 entry in ALL_GPU_DATABASES.
    scripts/build/miopen.sh installs only libMIOpen.so. At run time, MIOpen
    reads its system databases from share/miopen/db next to that library, and
    those come from the base image. The base image's MIOpen package installs
    databases only for MIOPEN_INSTALL_GPU_DATABASES, which is set to the
    TheRock target list, and that list has no gfx803. So no ROCm 10.x image
    from this repo ships a gfx803 find-db. Restoring the files in the source
    tree changes nothing at run time. Shipping them would change the
    immediate-mode solver choice for each of the 46002 problem records they
    list, and that is not what this patch restores.

winograd-fused-conv-miscompute.patch edits conv_bin_winoRxS_fused.cpp, so it
applies after this patch.

Applies to: MIOpen @ rocm-libraries release/therock-10.2, commit
8faffed0f978198ccf6fcfbd57e8db6afc83f35f. gfx803 only: each restored branch
is gated on the gfx803 device name, so no other architecture changes.

NOT YET RE-VERIFIED ON REAL HARDWARE on ROCm 10.2. Run these checks on the
card, in a container of the image that this pin builds:

  sh /work/tools/correctness-suite/build.sh /tmp/suite-bin /opt/rocm
  ONLY="conv:ConvBinWinograd3x3U conv:ConvBinWinogradRxS" \
      sh /work/tools/correctness-suite/run_all.sh /tmp/suite-bin /tmp/suite-results

Both sweeps must report the solver as applicable and 0 WRONG. Then run
MIOpenDriver's own GPU-against-CPU check with each restored solver forced. Use
-F 1 for forward and -F 2 for backward data:

  MIOPEN_DEBUG_FIND_ONLY_SOLVER=ConvBinWinograd3x3U MIOPEN_FIND_MODE=normal \
      MIOpenDriver conv -n 16 -c 64 -H 56 -W 56 -k 64 -y 3 -x 3 -p 1 -q 1 \
      -u 1 -v 1 -F 1 -V 1
  MIOPEN_DEBUG_FIND_ONLY_SOLVER=ConvBinWinogradRxS MIOPEN_FIND_MODE=normal \
      MIOpenDriver conv -n 16 -c 64 -H 56 -W 56 -k 64 -y 3 -x 3 -p 1 -q 1 \
      -u 1 -v 1 -F 2 -V 1

For the fused solver, run the same shape through MIOpenDriver CBAInfer with -V 1
and MIOPEN_LOG_LEVEL=6. The log must name ConvBinWinogradRxSFused. MIOpenDriver
comes from the base image, because this build turns MIOPEN_BUILD_DRIVER off. It
loads the libMIOpen.so that this build installs.

